.TH FATHOM_DAEMON_START 1  "fathom 0.1.0-alpha.1" 
.SH NAME
fathom\-daemon\-start \- Take the writer lease and watch this repository from this process, or from a detached one
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBfathom daemon start\fR [\fB\-\-root\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-foreground\fR] [\fB\-\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-require\-socket\fR] [\fB\-\-supervisor\fR] [\fB\-\-cpu\-share\-pct\fR] [\fB\-\-slice\fR] [\fB\-\-yield\-slice\fR] [\fB\-\-queue\-depth\fR] [\fB\-\-hook\-bytes\fR] [\fB\-\-backend\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-debounce\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-heartbeat\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-worktree\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-status\-file\fR] [\fB\-\-deadline\fR] [\fB\-\-max\-cycles\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Take the writer lease and watch this repository from this process, or from a detached one
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-root\fR \fI<ROOT>\fR [default: .]
The repository to watch and index
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print the health document as JSON instead of lines, and print it once the first pass has run
.TP
\fB\-\-quiet\fR
Print nothing but the health document; the heartbeat file is still written
.TP
\fB\-\-foreground\fR
Run in this process, so a supervisor can supervise it (`e6.3`, ADR\-004 §7.1).

This is the form systemd, a container `init` and a CI step want: stdout and stderr stay attached, and the process leaves on SIGTERM the same way it leaves on `fathom daemon stop`. Without it, `start` spawns the detached form and waits for its socket to answer.
.TP
\fB\-\-socket\fR \fI<PATH>\fR
Where to listen, instead of the endpoint derived from the repository (ADR\-004 §7.2)
.TP
\fB\-\-require\-socket\fR
Refuse to start rather than run with no IPC endpoint.

Off by default, because a filesystem that cannot host a socket (an SMB share, some container bind mount) is a reason to publish less, not a reason to have no daemon: the lease and the heartbeat file still answer `fathom status`.
.TP
\fB\-\-supervisor\fR \fI<SUPERVISOR>\fR
Who is supervising this daemon, recorded in the health document (`systemd`, `docker`, `ci`)
.TP
\fB\-\-cpu\-share\-pct\fR \fI<CPU_SHARE_PCT>\fR [default: 25]
The CPU ceiling, as a percent of one core. 25 is ADR\-004 §7.2\*(Aqs background default
.TP
\fB\-\-slice\fR \fI<SLICE>\fR [default: 2000]
Analysis units per pass while nothing is talking to the daemon
.TP
\fB\-\-yield\-slice\fR \fI<YIELD_SLICE>\fR [default: 50]
Analysis units per pass while a foreground client has just been heard — the yield slice
.TP
\fB\-\-queue\-depth\fR \fI<QUEUE_DEPTH>\fR [default: 64]
How many distinct index requests may wait before new ones are refused rather than queued
.TP
\fB\-\-hook\-bytes\fR \fI<HOOK_BYTES>\fR [default: 1048576]
Harness\-stream bytes per pass — the back\-pressure knob of ADR\-005 §6.5
.TP
\fB\-\-backend\fR \fI<BACKEND>\fR [default: auto]
Which change source to use: `auto`, `notify` or `poll`. The daemon is a watcher, so it takes the watcher\*(Aqs flags for the same meaning
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR \fI<INTERVAL_MS>\fR
The debounced polling interval in milliseconds
.TP
\fB\-\-debounce\-ms\fR \fI<DEBOUNCE_MS>\fR
The quiescence window in milliseconds
.TP
\fB\-\-heartbeat\-ms\fR \fI<HEARTBEAT_MS>\fR
The liveness beat in milliseconds, for the heartbeat file and the lease
.TP
\fB\-\-worktree\fR
Also re\-index uncommitted paths when only git\*(Aqs index moved
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-status\-file\fR
Do not write `.fathom/watch/status.json`
.TP
\fB\-\-deadline\fR \fI<DEADLINE>\fR
Stop after this many seconds — the supervisor\*(Aqs `TimeoutStopSec` seam and a test\*(Aqs
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-cycles\fR \fI<MAX_CYCLES>\fR
Stop after this many loop passes. A test seam, and the way to use the daemon as a one\-shot indexer
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
